      "proposition": {
        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "<p>In its final report the High Pay Centre says the median remuneration of a FTSE 100 CEO has risen to a record £5.06m</p><p>The bosses of Britain’s largest listed companies received record pay last year, fuelling the widest earnings gap with workers in eight years.</p><p>Median pay for FTSE 100 chief executives hit £5.06m in the last financial year, according to data released by the High Pay Centre, an 8.6% increase on £4.66m the previous year and the highest level on record.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/jul/20/uk-bosses-130-times-high-pay-worker-gap-widens\">Continue reading...</a>"
